# HAMR project .gitignore
# Ignores regenerable build output and tool scratch; keeps sources, requirements,
# reports, and verification evidence tracked.

# --- Build artifacts (Rust crates, Slang/JVM) ---
**/target/
**/out/

# --- Sireum / HAMR working & scratch artifacts ---
.slang/
.claude.out
**/microkit.system.merged
stale_outputs_checked
*.cmd.jar
*.cmd.com

# --- IDE / editor / OS ---
**/.metals/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.bloop/
**/.bsp/
**/.metadata/
**/.settings/
**/.scala-build/
**/.cache/
.fleet/
.DS_Store
compile_commands.json
*.aaxl2

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored (tracked as deliverables / evidence) ---
#   reports/                     workflow-status, change reports, contract audits
#   integration_constraints/     Logika integration-constraint verification evidence
#   hamr/microkit/attestation/   codegen attestation reports
# Do not add a broad *.json ignore -- it would hide real reports such as
# hamr/microkit/reporting/codegen_report_sysml.json.
